{"styles":[{"sc":"#ff2600","so":1,"w":2,"ol":true,"fc":"#fffb00","fo":0.502}],"cards":["<div style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#222222;max-width:238px;\"><div style=\"background:#0e7d46;height:6px;border-radius:3px 3px 0 0;\"></div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:7px 0 0;\">COUNTY BOUNDARY</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#0e7d46;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;padding:0 0 2px;\">GEORGIA</div><div style=\"font-size:16px;font-weight:800;padding:2px 0 6px;\">Clayton County</div><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;\"><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Population</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">297,703 (2024 est.)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">County Seat</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">Jonesboro</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Land Area</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">142 sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Density</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">2,096 / sq mi</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Household Income</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$60,067</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#666666;padding:3px 10px 3px 0;white-space:nowrap;\">Median Home Value</td><td style=\"color:#111111;font-weight:600;\">$264,900</td></tr></table><div style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#333333;padding:8px 0 2px;border-top:1px solid #eef2f1;margin-top:7px;\">Clayton County sits immediately south of Atlanta and is defined economically by Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport, whose footprint and workforce — including Delta Air Lines' Technical Operations base — anchor a logistics-driven economy where supply chain, warehousing, and air cargo account for a large share of local jobs. Forest Park and the Clayton-side edge of College Park have built out extensive industrial and distribution space feeding off airport access and the convergence of I-75, I-285, and I-675. Jonesboro, the county seat, retains a historic small-town core, while Riverdale, Morrow, and Lake City offer more conventional suburban retail and residential product. Incomes and home values trail the metro Atlanta average, making the county a value-oriented market for both industrial and workforce housing investment, with e-commerce and air-cargo growth continuing to drive demand for logistics space near the airport.</div><div style=\"font-size:11px;color:#888888;padding-top:6px;\">Source: U.S. Census Bureau · Data verified: September 13, 2026</div></div>"],"feats":[["Clayton",0,[[33.59643,-84.45818],[33.61534,-84.45808],[33.62294,-84.45799],[33.62465,-84.45801],[33.62702,-84.45795],[33.63014,-84.45797],[33.63138,-84.45794],[33.64222,-84.45787],[33.64887,-84.45788],[33.64887,-84.45309],[33.6477,-84.4532],[33.64405,-84.453],[33.6433,-84.453],[33.64161,-84.4531],[33.64109,-84.4531],[33.6411,-84.4483],[33.6422,-84.4482],[33.6436,-84.4482],[33.6457,-84.4486],[33.6467,-84.4484],[33.6467,-84.4458],[33.6487,-84.4458],[33.64879,-84.4458],[33.64881,-84.44577],[33.64876,-84.43809],[33.64878,-84.41898],[33.64862,-84.40874],[33.64823,-84.40874],[33.64833,-84.39114],[33.64832,-84.37999],[33.64795,-84.35015],[33.64792,-84.34674],[33.64794,-84.34122],[33.64779,-84.3298],[33.64731,-84.28165],[33.64565,-84.28156],[33.64556,-84.28152],[33.64531,-84.28151],[33.64398,-84.28148],[33.64151,-84.28156],[33.63982,-84.28145],[33.63937,-84.28146],[33.6393,-84.2798],[33.63923,-84.27186],[33.63121,-84.27206],[33.631,-84.26257],[33.62902,-84.26272],[33.62693,-84.26277],[33.62495,-84.26278],[33.62449,-84.26274],[33.62325,-84.26281],[33.61463,-84.26293],[33.61312,-84.26292],[33.61303,-84.26296],[33.6125,-8